  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing for impact against malaria - Haiti (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Haiti, Malaria, Population Services International (PSI HQ)This program has the following goals: To enable malaria to be completely eliminated from Haiti by 2022, so that the only diagnosed cases will be introduced cases. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: Confirm all suspected malaria cases by microscopy or RDT.  Objective 2: Correctly treat 100 percent of positive cases diagnosed by microscopy or RDT according to the national protocol.  Objective 3: Raise awareness among 80 percent of populations in at-risk areas about malaria transmission methods, the use of individual protection measures and participation in community-based activities to control malaria.  Objective 4: Implement an effective system of passive and active surveillance and epidemiological data about malaria in Haiti to enable sound decision-making.  Objective 5: Identify and appropriately treat all malaria outbreak areas (100 percent).  Objective 6: Implement an effective monitoring and evaluation system to make available epidemiological data and enable a selection of effective, relevant and targeted interventions.  Objective 7: Put in place an effective prediction, early warning and response system for epidemics.  Objective 8: Introduce appropriate changes to the national health system relevant to the administrative, technological and financial aspects of malaria elimination in Haiti.  Objective 9: Define and set up an administrative and legal framework for the NMCP with a view to eliminating malaria in Haiti</narrative>
  </description>
